# pubsub-state recovery — {{ inventory_hostname }} (standby)

This host keeps a **warm checkout** of the `{{ pubsub_state_checkout_org }}/{{ pubsub_state_checkout_repo }}`
Forgejo repo and a **staged `pubsub-apply` binary**, refreshed every
{{ pubsub_state_checkout_interval_sec }}s by `pubsub-state-pull.timer`. This is
the recovery side of Block 86 (`docs/design/pubsub-state-as-code.md`).

- Warm checkout : `{{ pubsub_state_checkout_dir }}/repo/`  (MANIFEST.yaml + vendors/ at its root)
- Staged binary : `{{ pubsub_state_apply_binary_dest }}`
- Last pull     : `journalctl -u pubsub-state-pull.service -n 5`

## On failover (do NOT run routinely — pubsub-apply MUTATES the portal)

After this node is promoted to active and its **own** `goat-zenoh-portal` is up,
restore the fabric structure from the local checkout:

```bash
# 1. Resolve this node's portal (container-network only; not host-published):
PIP=$(sudo docker inspect goat-zenoh-portal \
  -f '{{ '{{' }} (index .NetworkSettings.Networks "mgmt").IPAddress {{ '}}' }}')

# 2. Dry-run first — prints the plan, exits non-zero if anything would change:
{{ pubsub_state_apply_binary_dest }} \
  -from {{ pubsub_state_checkout_dir }}/repo \
  -portal-url "http://$PIP:8090" \
  -api-key "${{ site_id | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_PUBSUB_MIRROR_PORTAL_KEY" \
  -dry-run

# 3. Execute (creates missing vendors → re-mints certs/bundles, topics,
#    schemas, examples; retires/deletes what the repo no longer has):
{{ pubsub_state_apply_binary_dest }} \
  -from {{ pubsub_state_checkout_dir }}/repo \
  -portal-url "http://$PIP:8090" \
  -api-key "${{ site_id | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_PUBSUB_MIRROR_PORTAL_KEY"
```

`${{ site_id | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_PUBSUB_MIRROR_PORTAL_KEY` is the `pubsub-state-mirror` service
operator key. If it is not in the failover shell's env, use any operator key
present in this node's `/opt/goat-zenoh-portal/operator-keys.d/` (strip the
`handle:` prefix — the `-api-key` value is the part after the colon).

## If Forgejo (Orin-C) was also lost

Fall back to the MinIO backup tier, then apply from the extracted tree:

```bash
mc cp {{ pubsub_state_minio_alias | default('local-' ~ site_id) }}/pubsub-state-snapshots/latest.tar.gz /tmp/
mkdir -p /tmp/pubsub-restore && tar xzf /tmp/latest.tar.gz -C /tmp/pubsub-restore
# the tarball's top dir is pubsub-state/ :
{{ pubsub_state_apply_binary_dest }} -from /tmp/pubsub-restore/pubsub-state -portal-url "http://$PIP:8090" -api-key "$KEY" -dry-run
```
